NAME
       cmp - compare two files byte by byte

SYNOPSIS
       cmp [-s] [-l] FILE1 FILE2

DESCRIPTION
       cmp reads two files side by side and reports the first byte and line
       where they differ:

           a.txt b.txt differ: byte 12, line 2

       It says nothing when the files are the same. The exit status is 0 for
       identical files, 1 when they differ and 2 on trouble, so it works well
       in if statements. Use diff to see what changed in text files.

OPTIONS
       -s, --quiet, --silent
              Print nothing; only set the exit status.

       -l     List every differing byte, not just the first.

EXAMPLES
           if cmp -s /etc/hosts /root/hosts.bak; then echo same; fi

SEE ALSO
       diff(1), comm(1), cksum(1)
